	"buildings": {
		"note": "Height rule: a lot's height comes from its district type and its distance from the core centre. Each type has a min_height (far from the core), a max_height (at the core centre) and a reach (the distance at which the height has fallen to min_height); falloff_power bends the curve (higher = the peak is more concentrated). A seeded variation of up to +/- `variation` is then applied, and the result snaps to whole floors of floor_height. coverage = share of the lot a building fills; setback = gap kept from the lot edge. No building may exceed height_cap_fraction of the main landmark. Special sites get the fixed heights in `sites` (0 = left open). Lots that hold a landmark stay empty for the landmark itself.",
